<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Dec numbers in work fall to 34.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Dec numbers in work fall to 34.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN NUMBERS IN WORK		 Dec 96   Nov 96   Dec 95</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(unadj, million)    34.307   34.474   34.809</p>
<p> Number in work (1)(seas adj, million) 34.199   34.246   34.697</p>
<p> Number in work (2)(seas adj, million) 34.239   34.285   34.739</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj,million)	  28.087   28.221   28.446</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)    28.020   28.043   28.378</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN</p>
<p> Number in work (unadj, million)	  6.249    6.295    6.934</p>
<p> Number in work (seas adj, million)     6.219    6.242    6.361</p>
<p>NOTE - Pan-German figure marked (1) refer to people living in Germany. Those marked (2), as well as all the west and east German figures, refer to people working in the respective regions but not necessarily living in Germany.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
